bypass: 66
rule: ASSERT_WEAKENED
issue: 325
title: touching a runner script that runs `py.test` is not production repair evidence
origin: issue #325. A script whose only runner was `py.test` was no test command, so it stayed production, and one line of it bought the opaque exemption that held the weakened assertion beside it at warn. v0.6.0 passes it; the same diff on `pytest` blocks (runner_script_cannot_disarm_pos)
=== before: scripts/test.sh ===
#!/usr/bin/env bash
set -euo pipefail
py.test -q
=== after: scripts/test.sh ===
#!/usr/bin/env bash
set -euo pipefail
py.test -q --maxfail=1
=== before: tests/test_billing.py ===
from app.billing import invoice_total


def test_invoice_total():
    assert invoice_total([{"price": 50.0, "qty": 2}], 0.053) == 105.3
=== after: tests/test_billing.py ===
from app.billing import invoice_total


def test_invoice_total():
    assert invoice_total([{"price": 50.0, "qty": 2}], 0.053) > 0
